THOUGHT: `instructions` is a nullable field (set to null in `unloadInsnArr()`), so `getInstructions()` returning it violates a @NonNull contract. Since other methods like `getArgTypes()` throw if uninitialized rather than returning null, the consistent fix is to enforce non-null here by throwing when `instructions` is null, instead of changing annotations. I’ll update `getInstructions()` accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '306,309c\	public InsnNode[] getInstructions() {
		if (instructions == null) {
			throw new JadxRuntimeException("Method instructions not loaded: " + this);
		}
		return instructions;
	}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/nodes/MethodNode.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway: .*errors" -n new_build_output.log || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

